hi my name is Yu Feng Guo and today  we're going to explore how you can build  a solution with Google Cloud AI by  taking a look at the use case of using  AI and manufacturing for increased  productivity our example comes from the  machining industry so let's first talk a  bit about what machining is machining is  the process for cutting raw materials  such as metal wood or plastic into a  desired final shape in size modern  machine shops use computer-controlled  precision machining tools for operations  like cutting drilling boring milling and  so on machining is an essential part of  the manufacturing industry historically  a major challenge of the machining  industry is the time-consuming task of  cost estimation for instance when a  machine shop takes an order for building  parts like these it needs to determine  the individual cuts and holes that need  to be made for each individual part by  carefully reading the blueprint provided  by the customer  this manual process requires machining  experts who are dedicated to the cost  estimation process which can act as a  bottleneck for the productivity of the  machine shop as a whole a company called  kibou qu in Japan has launched a new  solution for this challenge by handling  the data management of their machining  process with AI kibou qu is a start-up  focused on modernizing the manufacturing  industry with 3d printing cloud and AI  technologies for major manufacturing  customers including Toyota Honda and  Olympus let's see how Kabu cooze data  management tool works first a blueprint  is uploaded to the tool in the web  browser and a region is specified for  estimation then the user simply presses  the cost estimation button the tool  detects and highlights every object that  requires processing you can see the  detected types of processing steps how  many there are how much each costs and  the total estimated cost for the entire  part the tool also allows users to add  detailed info for each part or to have  experts update any part that requires  minor fixes the tool can detect tens of  processing parts on the design in less  than one second which significantly  increases the productivity of cost  estimation by machining experts  Masahiko Adashi CEO of kabuki explains  the benefit of this tool if machine  shops can respond quickly to cost  estimation requests from their customers  that's a better customer experience and  more business opportunities additionally  this tool can act as a central  repository of expert knowledge for each  machine shop this allows the shop to  easily share knowledge with junior staff  members and learners without any  bottlenecks and make business operations  much more scalable let's learn more  about how kabuki built this tool with  the power of Google Cloud AI kabuki tool  was able to detect the machining  operations from the blueprint to achieve  this they used our auto amel vision  technology with object detection first  they collected thousands of images in  preparation for ML model training with  different labelled blueprints for  drilling boring and cutting operations  on them usually it would take a lot of  time to build an object detection system  using their training data for production  use you would need to start with data  pre-processing ml model design hyper  parameter tuning evaluation and  deployment and would also need to have  resources to keep the model up-to-date  and that would require hiring a experts  and ml engineers for faster  time-to-market Kabukicho zaur Auto ml  technology which automates many steps in  the ML lifecycle all they had to do was  upload their training images to Auto ml  vision and press the train button to  start the automated model training and  development process  [Music]  in half a day they got an object  detection model generated by auto mail  vision with a detailed report for the  model accuracy and various metrics then  kabuki downloaded the ML model and used  it with tensorflow J s which allows you  to run the object detection within a web  browser that's the reason why Kabu cooze  machining data management tool is able  to detect tens of processing parts in  just one second even though you could  build the object detection model much  faster with Auto ml vision that's not  the whole story  one important requirement for a kabuki  tool is the ability to keep learning  from the experts the practices and  patterns used in blueprints are  different for each customer project or  machining expert so the tool provides a  UI for fixing the missed detected parts  or adding more details based on this  feedback from experts the tool reruns  the ML training process and deploys a  better ml model that captures the  practices and patterns use in each case  [Music]  to implement this continuous ml training  process kibou KU used cloud a AI  platform pipelines this product allows  users to build orchestrated ml pipelines  and manage them from data pre-processing  and validation all the way through to  model training validation and deployment  instead of asking AI experts again and  again for a manual rerun of the whole  training process everything can be  automated and continuously integrated  just by invoking the pipeline making the  whole service robust and production  ready with a high platform pipelines  seppuku was able to build a positive  feedback loop between the machining  experts and model training pipeline  resulting in ever better accuracy of  their model and higher productivity as  the experts keep using the tool this  loop of application and training is  called active learning in ml in summary  kabuki was able to use the power of  Google Cloud AI for faster  time-to-market quick abject detection  and create a flexible ml pipeline for  active learning what will your AI  journey look like get started today with  these tools from Google Cloud AI  you  [Music]
 

